      assign handle_diet = 'Vegetarian'
      assign handle_chef_notes = 'Always bloom pure coriander powder in warm ghee or oil for 20 seconds before adding liquids — raw dhana powder can taste dusty if not gently heated in fat.'
      assign handle_featured_product_handles = 'dhana-powder'
      assign handle_ingredients = '[Ingredients]||2 tsp DV Gold Pure Dhana (Coriander) Powder||3 potatoes (boiled & diced)||1 tbsp pure desi ghee||1 tsp cumin seeds (jeera)||1 tsp amchur (dry mango powder)||1 green chilli (chopped)||Salt to taste and fresh coriander'
      assign handle_instructions = 'Dhana Aloo Sabzi: Melt ghee, add cumin seeds and green chilli. Add boiled potato cubes and toss with 2 tsp DV Gold Dhana Powder, amchur, and salt. Saute until nicely crusted.||Fresh Coriander Chutney: Blend fresh green coriander, green chillies, lemon juice, and 1 tsp dhana powder for rich body and intense fresh herb flavor.||Vegetable Marinade: Whisk hung curd with dhana powder, kasuri methi, ginger-garlic paste, and lemon to marinate paneer or vegetables before grilling.||Dhana Tadka for Dal: Bloom 1 tsp dhana powder in hot ghee with cumin and hing for 20 seconds, pouring immediately over hot simmered yellow dal.||Spiced Buttermilk (Chaas): Whisk fresh chilled yogurt and water with roasted dhana powder, black salt, and mint leaves for a refreshing digestive drink.'
