      assign handle_diet = 'Vegetarian / Vegan'
      assign handle_chef_notes = 'Soak dried anjeer in warm milk or water for 15 minutes before blending — it rehydrates the fruit, making it effortlessly smooth while unlocking its natural caramel sweetness.'
      assign handle_featured_product_handles = 'anjeer-figs'
      assign handle_ingredients = '[Ingredients]||8-10 DV Gold Premium Anjeer (Dried Figs)||2 tbsp unsweetened almond or peanut butter||2 tbsp crushed DV Gold walnuts and pistachios||1 cup warm milk or water (for soaking)||¼ tsp cardamom powder||1 tbsp raw honey (optional)'
      assign handle_instructions = 'Stuffed Gourmet Anjeer: Gently slit plump DV Gold dried figs along the side. Fill with creamy almond or peanut butter and press crushed walnuts and pistachios inside for a luxurious healthy dessert bite.||Anjeer Energy Laddoos: Soak figs in warm water for 15 minutes, drain, and blend with roasted walnuts, cashews, and cardamom. Roll into bite-sized guilt-free sweets.||Creamy Anjeer Milkshake: Blend 4 soaked figs with 1 cup cold milk, 1 ripe banana, and a pinch of cinnamon into a velvety, fiber-rich shake.||Anjeer Overnight Oats: Layer rolled oats with chia seeds, milk, and chopped soaked anjeer. Leave in the fridge overnight for an effortless morning breakfast.||Anjeer & Nut Slices: Press chopped soaked figs firmly with chopped pistachios and walnuts into a cylinder shape; chill and slice into discs.||Tangy Anjeer Chutney: Simmer chopped figs with grated ginger, chilli flakes, cumin, and a splash of lemon juice until thick and jammy.||Anjeer Dessert Toast: Spread hung curd or ricotta on toasted sourdough, arrange sliced anjeer, and top with crushed pistachios and honey.'
